<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="38f089db">&lt;p&gt;
    Scorecards are platforms to communicate progress to technology and business and enable key stakeholders to make
    informed decisions. Scorecards leverage key performance indicators (“KPIs”) and general summaries of data to assist in
    the management of performance. Additionally, a scorecard typically links back to plans so that the performance can be
    measured against intended targets.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Typically, a benefits scorecard displays graphic indicators that visually convey the overall success or failure in
    achieving intended benefits of a program or project. They are based on a collection of key performance indicators
    (KPIs) used to assess the realization of previously identified program or project benefits.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p/&gt;&lt;p&gt;
    Typically, the benefits dashboards and scorecard display graphic indicators that visually convey the overall success or
    failure in achieving intended benefits of a program or project. They are based on a collection of key performance
    indicators (KPIs) used to assess the realization of previously identified program or project benefits.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
